From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: calc, mspaint, snippingtool: system32 launchers for the App Paths programs

Windows has calc.exe, mspaint.exe and snippingtool.exe in system32, and
programs, scripts and the command line start them by name with
CreateProcess -- a search of system32 and the PATH that never reads App
Paths. Wine has none of them. These are the system32 (and syswow64) names:
each starts the program App Paths registers for its own file name --
sg-shell's Calculator, Paint and Snipping Tool -- with the same arguments,
and exits, as Windows 10's calc.exe is a launcher for the Calculator app.

The 32-bit copies read the 64-bit registry view, where App Paths are
registered. A target that is the launcher itself or sits in a system
directory is refused (no chain of launchers); with nothing registered they
say the program is not installed.

RegGetValue with RRF_RT_REG_EXPAND_SZ and no RRF_NOEXPAND fails with
ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER, as on Windows: RRF_RT_REG_SZ alone takes (and
expands) REG_EXPAND_SZ.

Gate: test/handoff-gate.sh.
